35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the scanning contractors slip when big clients book first, but bench tools ship fast! That’s a huge relief for our timeline worries.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, interesting. My records show the digitisation project stalled, but the partner groups thrived. I’m checking who actually supervises them now.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the technician who kept the power tools certified retired in spring. No one on the payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, that confirms the skill gap. @Benjamin, the grant only covers twelve months, then the flat budget takes over. That’s the structural weakness I see.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, the bus links are gone. Residents face an hour’s round trip. @Yumi, evening bookings are full, but remote use peaks after lock-up.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s heartbreaking! But @Benjamin, since the partner groups survived, maybe we can lean on them? I’m worried about relying on fragile supply chains.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the partner groups survived because they were self-sustaining, not because we managed them. We lack the supervision skills to replicate that success.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The associations train their own people, but we lack the certified supervisor to manage them. We can’t just assume the roster is ready.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, that aligns with my findings. The grant covers sessions for a year, then the flat budget absorbs them. That structural shift is where the strain begins.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, that timing gap is terrifying. If the money runs out, we can’t keep the doors open for people who can’t travel.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s so sad! But @Benjamin, since the partner groups survived, maybe we can lean on them? I’m worried about relying on fragile supply chains.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, leaning on them is risky. They survived because they were independent, not because we managed them. We lack the supervision skills to replicate that success.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. The associations are self-sufficient, but we lack the certified supervisor to manage them. We can’t just assume the roster is ready.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the vehicle line overran by a third, while equipment came in under. That mismatch signals where the flat budget will actually strain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, that overrun is worrying. But the bus loss is the real barrier. People can’t reach us if the roads are closed or the links are gone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, that vehicle overrun is scary! But @Daisuke, if the halls kept their timetables despite the closures, maybe we can find a stable, local anchor for our services?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the halls survived because they were local. A mobile unit faces the same winter closures. We’d be importing the problem, not solving it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the associations already staff their own sessions. We don’t need to supervise them; we need to stop assuming our roster can handle new technical roles.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun confirms the flat budget will strain on recurring costs. We must avoid proposals that rely on capital items the endowment can’t sustain.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if the halls stayed open, maybe we can partner with them? I’m worried about adding more strain to our already stretched staff.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
