61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the archive failed because we tried to manage it centrally. The partner groups succeeded because they were independent. We should follow the model that actually worked.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the archive failed due to central management. The associations succeeded because they are self-sufficient. We lack the certified supervisors to manage new external facilitators.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the grant covers sessions for twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs them. That structural shift is where the strain begins.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The bus loss is the real barrier. A mobile unit faces the same winter closures. We’d be importing the problem, not solving it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I love that the partner groups worked! But @Shion, if we lack supervisors, how do we safely start new circles? I’m worried about the skill gap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the circles rely on partner organizations to provide the trained facilitators. We don’t need to supervise them; we just need to coordinate. That’s the model that survived.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, coordination is still a commitment. If the partner facilitators fail, who absorbs the gap? We have no trained backup on the roster to step in.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, valid concern. But the grant covers session fees for twelve months. The flat budget then carries them. We must ensure the recurring cost fits the long-term structure, not just the initial grant.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I worry about the physical reach. If we rely on partners, do they actually travel to the outer wards where the bus links are gone?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s a great point! If partners can’t reach the outer wards, we’re stuck. @Minako, does the grant cover travel costs for them?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, the partner groups already meet in local venues. We don’t need to travel; we just need to coordinate. That solves the access problem without adding vehicle costs.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, coordination is still a commitment. If the partner facilitators fail, who absorbs the gap? We have no trained backup on the roster to step in.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, coordination is cheaper than vehicles, but the flat budget still absorbs the recurring fees. We must verify the long-term cost fits our structure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, that helps. But if they meet locally, do they actually reach the outer wards where the bus links are gone?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I’m leaning toward the Language Circles! The partner model feels stable, and it avoids the winter road risks. @Daisuke, do you think they can reach the outer wards?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the records show they met in local venues, not our branches. If they don’t cover the outer wards, we haven’t solved the access gap.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. If they don’t cover the outer wards, we haven’t solved the access gap. I vote for C, but only if we verify the partner coverage first.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, I agree. The recurring fees must fit the flat budget. I vote for C, provided the partner coverage is verified.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
